Article 1 An Intellectual Property Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance cases within its municipal district:
(1) civil and administrative cases involving patents, new varieties of plants, layout designs of integrated circuits, technical secrets, and computer software;
(2) administrative cases filed against administrative actions of the State Council departments or local people's governments at or above the county level concerning copyrights, trademarks, unfair competition, etc.;
(3) civil cases involving the recognition of well-known trademarks.

Article 5 The Beijing Intellectual Property Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance administrative cases:
(1) cases brought against the rulings or decisions made by the State Council departments concerning the grant and affirmation of rights of patents, trademarks, new varieties of plants, layout designs of integrated circuits, and other intellectual property;
(2) cases brought against the compulsory licensing decisions made by the State Council departments concerning patents, new varieties of plants, layout designs of integrated circuits, and the rulings on the fees or remuneration for compulsory licensing;
(3) cases brought against other administrative actions of the State Council departments concerning the grant and affirmation of intellectual property rights.
